# APML: Parallel Build System
# Version: 1.0.0 (2026-02-09)
# Status: Production
# Type: CORE (build infrastructure)
#
# Replaced sequential single-agent builds with a coordinator/sub-agent
# pattern using draft staging. The most significant architectural
# addition to the SSi Course Builder in Feb 2026.

core ParallelBuildSystem:
  name: "Parallel Build System"
  purpose: "Enable concurrent multi-agent seed decomposition with collision-safe finalization"
  version: "1.0.0"
  status: "Production"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## OVERVIEW
  ## ==========================================================================

  overview:
    title: "Why Parallel Builds Exist"

    problem: |
      Sequential builds (one agent, one seed at a time) are slow.
      A 300-seed course at ~2 minutes per seed takes ~10 hours.
      A 668-seed course takes over 22 hours.
      A single agent crash means restarting from the last checkpoint.

    solution: |
      Parallel builds split the work across multiple sub-agents (up to 10)
      running concurrently. Each agent works on an independent batch of seeds
      and submits to a DRAFT staging table rather than directly to live tables.
      When all drafts are in, a finalization pass processes them in seed order,
      detecting ZUT collisions between agents and deduplicating LEGOs.

    benefits:
      - "Speed: 10 agents reduce a 10-hour build to ~1-2 hours"
      - "Resilience: one agent crash only loses its batch, others continue"
      - "Collision safety: ZUT conflicts between agents are caught at finalize, not silently introduced"
      - "Visibility: dashboard shows real-time draft/finalize/collision status per seed"
      - "Resumability: restart skips seeds that already have valid drafts"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## ARCHITECTURE
  ## ==========================================================================

  architecture:
    title: "Coordinator / Sub-Agent / Draft Staging / Finalization"

    pattern: |
      The parallel build uses a three-tier architecture:

      1. COORDINATOR AGENT (Sonnet model)
         - Spawned by the API via iTerm2 osascript or headless process
         - Does NOT build seeds itself
         - Uses Claude Code's Task tool to spawn ~10 background sub-agents
         - Polls /api/course/:code/drafts every 60s to monitor progress
         - Calls /api/course/:code/finalize when all drafts are submitted
         - Handles collision resolution by spawning fix sub-agents

      2. SUB-AGENTS (Sonnet model, ~10 concurrent)
         - Each receives a batch of seed numbers to decompose
         - Fetches seeds and vocabulary from the API
         - Submits each seed via POST /api/seed/complete?draft=true
         - Runs fully autonomous (no human interaction)
         - Retries on validation errors without limit

      3. DRAFT STAGING TABLE (course_seed_drafts)
         - Receives validated submissions from sub-agents
         - One draft per seed (UNIQUE constraint, upsert replaces)
         - Tracks validation_status: valid, collision, rework
         - Isolated from live tables until finalization

      4. FINALIZATION ENDPOINT (/api/course/:code/finalize)
         - Processes drafts in seed order (ascending)
         - Deduplicates LEGOs (same known + same target = duplicate)
         - Detects collisions (same known + different target = ZUT violation)
         - On collision: aborts, marks affected drafts, reports resolution steps
         - On clean: writes to live tables, deletes drafts

    diagram: |
      Dashboard                    Course Builder API (port 3471)
         |                                    |
         |  POST /api/build/start/:code       |
         +----------------------------------->|
         |                                    |
         |    Spawns Coordinator Agent         |
         |    (iTerm2 or headless)             |
         |                                    |
         |         Coordinator                 |
         |            |                        |
         |            | Task tool (x10)        |
         |            +----+----+----+         |
         |            |    |    |    |         |
         |           SA1  SA2  SA3  ...       |
         |            |    |    |    |         |
         |            | POST /api/seed/complete?draft=true
         |            +----+----+----+-------->|
         |                                    |
         |                          course_seed_drafts
         |                                    |
         |            Coordinator polls       |
         |            GET /drafts             |
         |            <-----------------------|
         |                                    |
         |            POST /finalize          |
         |            +---------------------->|
         |                                    |
         |                          course_seeds / course_legos /
         |                          course_practice_phrases (live)

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## DATABASE SCHEMA
  ## ==========================================================================

  database:
    title: "Draft Staging and Build Job Tracking"

    course_seed_drafts:
      migration: "database/migrations/20260207_course_seed_drafts.sql"
      purpose: "Staging table for parallel agent submissions before finalization"

      columns:
        id:
          type: "UUID"
          default: "gen_random_uuid()"
          note: "Primary key"
        course_code:
          type: "TEXT NOT NULL"
          references: "courses(course_code)"
        seed_number:
          type: "INTEGER NOT NULL"
        known_text:
          type: "TEXT NOT NULL"
          note: "English seed sentence"
        target_text:
          type: "TEXT NOT NULL"
          note: "Target language seed sentence"
        submission_data:
          type: "JSONB NOT NULL"
          note: "Full parsed legos array with build/use phrases"
          structure: |
            {
              "legos": [
                {
                  "idx": 1, "type": "A",
                  "known": "...", "target": "...",
                  "build": [...], "use": [...]
                },
                ...
              ]
            }
        validation_status:
          type: "TEXT"
          default: "'valid'"
          check: "IN ('valid', 'collision', 'rework')"
          note: "Set to 'collision' by finalize when ZUT conflict detected"
        validation_notes:
          type: "JSONB"
          note: "Collision details, validation timestamps, skipped checks"
        created_at:
          type: "TIMESTAMPTZ"
          default: "NOW()"
        updated_at:
          type: "TIMESTAMPTZ"
          default: "NOW()"

      constraints:
        unique: "UNIQUE(course_code, seed_number) — one draft per seed, upsert replaces"

      indexes:
        - "idx_course_seed_drafts_course ON (course_code)"
        - "idx_course_seed_drafts_status ON (course_code, validation_status)"

      rls:
        service_role: "full access (API server uses service_role key)"
        authenticated: "read-only (dashboard viewing)"

    build_jobs_build_mode:
      migration: "database/migrations/20260208_add_build_mode_to_build_jobs.sql"
      purpose: "Tracks whether a build is sequential or parallel"

      column:
        name: "build_mode"
        type: "TEXT"
        default: "'parallel'"
        comment: "Build strategy: parallel (coordinator + sub-agents via drafts)"
        note: "Added to existing build_jobs table. Default is parallel — sequential mode is legacy."

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## WORKFLOW: BUILD START TO FINALIZATION
  ## ==========================================================================

  workflow:
    title: "Step-by-Step Parallel Build Lifecycle"

    step_1:
      name: "Build Start"
      trigger: "POST /api/build/start/:courseCode"
      params:
        terminal: "'iTerm2' (default) or headless"
        targetSeeds: "668 (default) — how many seeds to build"
      actions:
        - "Check for existing running/stalled build_jobs record for this course"
        - "If running: reject ('Build already running')"
        - "If stalled: resume existing job (update status to running)"
        - "If none: create new build_jobs record with build_mode='parallel'"
        - "Start the build manager (stall watcher)"
        - "Call spawnParallelBuildAgent()"

    step_2:
      name: "Smart Batch Assignment"
      function: "spawnParallelBuildAgent()"
      actions:
        - "Query course_seed_drafts for existing valid drafts"
        - "Query course_seeds for already-finalized seeds (decomposed_at IS NOT NULL)"
        - "Build seedsNeeded list: seeds 11..targetSeeds minus drafted minus finalized"
        - "Split into up to 10 batches (min 20 seeds per batch)"
        - "Fetch golden decomposition examples from quality_rules"
        - "Fetch build_lessons for the language family"
        - "Generate coordinator brief with batch assignments and methodology"
        - "Write brief to /tmp/claude_parallel_{courseCode}_{timestamp}.txt"
        - "Spawn coordinator agent (iTerm2 osascript or headless child_process)"

    step_3:
      name: "Coordinator Spawns Sub-Agents"
      actor: "Coordinator agent"
      actions:
        - "Parse batch assignments from its brief"
        - "Use Claude Code's Task tool to spawn one background sub-agent per batch"
        - "All batches launched in parallel (single message with multiple Task calls)"
        - "Each sub-agent prompt contains: seed list, API endpoints, methodology, golden examples, JSON template"

    step_4:
      name: "Sub-Agent Decomposition"
      actor: "Each sub-agent"
      loop: "For each seed in its assigned batch"
      actions:
        - "Fetch seed data from GET /api/seeds/:courseCode"
        - "Fetch vocabulary from GET /api/vocab/:courseCode"
        - "Decompose seed into LEGOs (A-type and M-type)"
        - "Write BUILD phrases (min 3 per LEGO) and USE phrases (min 8 per LEGO)"
        - "Submit via POST /api/seed/complete?draft=true"
        - "On validation error: read error, fix, resubmit (no retry limit)"
        - "On success: proceed to next seed"

    step_5:
      name: "Draft Validation (Server-Side)"
      trigger: "POST /api/seed/complete with ?draft=true"
      validations_run:
        - "Tiling: seed target constructable from LEGO targets"
        - "Vocabulary: phrases only use introduced vocabulary (from prior seed translations)"
        - "Build/Use format: correct phrase structure and counts"
        - "Phrase counts: minimum BUILD and USE per LEGO"
        - "Complexity and length ratio checks"
      validations_skipped:
        - "ZUT: cannot know what other parallel agents have created (deferred to finalize)"
        - "Balance: LEGO count balance (advisory only)"
      on_pass: |
        Upsert into course_seed_drafts with validation_status='valid'.
        validation_notes records which checks passed and which were skipped.
        Returns { status: 'DRAFTED', action: 'PROCEED TO NEXT SEED' }.
      vocabulary_strategy: |
        For parallel builds, vocabulary is derived from seed translations (target_text
        of seeds 1..N-1) rather than from course_legos (which may not exist yet for
        parallel seeds). This works because LEGOs must tile their seed translation,
        so word-level vocab from translations equals word-level vocab from LEGOs.
        Also includes vocab from existing LEGOs in live tables (golden seeds 1-10).

    step_6:
      name: "Coordinator Monitors Progress"
      actor: "Coordinator agent"
      endpoint: "GET /api/course/:code/drafts"
      actions:
        - "Poll every 60 seconds via curl"
        - "Response: { total_drafts, valid, collision, rework, drafts: [...] }"
        - "When total_drafts >= targetSeeds - 10 (golden seeds excluded), proceed to finalize"
        - "If progress stalls (no new drafts for 10 minutes), report issue"

    step_7:
      name: "Dashboard Shows Seed Grid"
      endpoint: "GET /api/build/seed-grid/:courseCode"
      ui_component: "TextGeneration.vue"
      statuses:
        complete: "green (bg-emerald-500/80) — seed finalized in live tables"
        drafted: "amber (bg-amber-500/80) — valid draft in staging table"
        collision: "red (bg-red-500/80) — ZUT collision detected at finalize"
        rework: "red (bg-red-500/80) — marked for rework"
        building: "default — has LEGOs but not yet decomposed_at"
        empty: "grey (bg-slate-700/80) — no content yet"
      display: |
        Grid of 5x5px colored cells, one per seed.
        Header shows: "{finalized}/{total} finalized", "{drafted} drafted", "{collision} collision".
        Hover tooltip: "S{N}: {status} ({legos}L, {phrases}P)".
        Legend: Empty | Drafted | Collision | Finalized.

    step_8:
      name: "Finalization"
      trigger: "POST /api/course/:code/finalize"
      steps:
        step_8a:
          name: "Load Baseline"
          action: |
            Load all existing LEGOs from live tables (course_legos).
            Build known_text -> { target_text, seed_number, lego_index } map
            from is_new=true LEGOs. This is the baseline vocabulary from
            golden seeds (1-10) plus any previously finalized seeds.

        step_8b:
          name: "Load Drafts"
          action: |
            Load all drafts from course_seed_drafts in seed_number order.
            If no drafts found, return error with hint.

        step_8c:
          name: "Process Drafts — Dedup + Collision Detection"
          action: |
            For each draft in seed order, for each LEGO in the draft:
            1. Look up LEGO known text in the baseline map
            2. If found with SAME target: mark as DUPLICATE (dedup)
            3. If found with DIFFERENT target: mark as COLLISION (ZUT violation)
            4. If not found: mark as NEW, add to baseline map

            Track dedup counts, collision details, and empty seeds
            (seeds where all LEGOs are duplicates of earlier vocabulary).

        step_8d:
          name: "Collision Gate"
          action: |
            If any collisions found:
            - Update colliding drafts in DB to validation_status='collision'
            - Store collision details in validation_notes
            - Return HTTP 409 with collisions array and resolution steps
            - Finalization ABORTED — nothing written to live tables

        step_8e:
          name: "Write to Live Tables"
          condition: "Zero collisions"
          action: |
            For each draft in seed order:
            1. Upsert course_seeds with decomposed_at timestamp
            2. Upsert course_legos (is_new=false for duplicates)
            3. Generate and insert practice phrases (build-up, BUILD, USE)
            4. Handle empty seeds: attach seed sentence as USE phrase
               to the highest-indexed introducing LEGO from earlier seeds
            After all drafts written:
            5. Delete all drafts from course_seed_drafts
            6. Invalidate vocabulary cache

        step_8f:
          name: "Report"
          response: |
            {
              ok: true,
              status: 'FINALIZED',
              seeds_written, legos_introduced, legos_deduplicated,
              empty_seeds, phrases_written, collisions: 0
            }

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## COLLISION RESOLUTION
  ## ==========================================================================

  collision_resolution:
    title: "ZUT Conflict Detection and Resolution Between Parallel Agents"

    what_is_a_collision: |
      A collision occurs when two parallel agents independently choose the
      same English known text for a LEGO but map it to DIFFERENT target
      language translations. This violates ZUT (Zero Uncertainty Test):
      the learner must always know exactly what to produce.

      Example:
        Agent A (seed 45): "time" -> "temps" (French for weather/time)
        Agent B (seed 89): "time" -> "fois" (French for occurrence)
      Both are valid translations, but the learner cannot have two mappings.

    why_parallel_causes_collisions: |
      In sequential builds, ZUT is checked at submission time against the
      live LEGO table. Each agent sees all prior LEGOs.

      In parallel builds, ZUT checking at submission time is SKIPPED
      (isDraft=true bypasses the checkLegoConflict call) because agents
      cannot see each other's drafts. Collisions are deferred to finalization
      where all drafts are processed in seed order against a single baseline.

    detection: |
      During finalization (step_8c), each LEGO's known text is checked
      against the growing baseline map. If the same known text already
      exists with a different target_text (case-insensitive comparison),
      a collision is recorded with:
        - seed_number, lego_known, lego_target, lego_idx
        - conflicts_with: { target_text, seed_number, lego_index }

    resolution_workflow: |
      1. Finalize returns HTTP 409 with collisions array and colliding_seeds
      2. Coordinator queries GET /api/course/:code/drafts?status=collision
      3. Coordinator spawns fix sub-agents for colliding seeds
      4. Fix agents redecompose the seed using bigger M-LEGOs
         (absorb the ambiguous word into a context phrase so its
         English known text becomes unique)
      5. Fix agents resubmit via POST /api/seed/complete?draft=true
         (upsert replaces old draft)
      6. Coordinator calls POST /api/course/:code/finalize again
      7. Repeat until clean

    resolution_strategy: |
      The fix for a collision is to "upchunk" the ambiguous word into a
      larger M-LEGO where the English known text is unique:

      Before (collision):
        "time" -> "temps"     (seed 45)
        "time" -> "fois"      (seed 89)

      After (resolved):
        "the time" -> "le temps"       (seed 45, M-LEGO with context)
        "one time" -> "une fois"       (seed 89, M-LEGO with context)

      The English known texts are now different, so ZUT is satisfied.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## STALL DETECTION AND HEARTBEATS
  ## ==========================================================================

  stall_detection:
    title: "Monitoring Agent Health During Parallel Builds"

    constants:
      HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS: "3 * 60 * 1000 (3 minutes) — agent considered dead if no heartbeat"
      STALL_THRESHOLD_MS: "5 * 60 * 1000 (5 minutes) — course considered stalled if no submission"

    heartbeat_mechanism: |
      Agents send heartbeats in two ways:
      1. AUTO-HEARTBEAT: Every POST /api/seed/complete call automatically
         updates the agent heartbeat (agentHeartbeats map) with timestamp,
         current seed number, and status.
      2. MANUAL HEARTBEAT: POST /api/heartbeat/:courseCode — explicit
         keepalive with agent_id, status, and current_seed.

    stall_watcher: |
      The build manager runs a periodic stall watcher that checks build_jobs:
      1. Find jobs with status 'running' or 'stalled'
      2. Check last_heartbeat age against HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS
      3. If heartbeat fresh: agent alive, skip
      4. If heartbeat stale (>3 min): mark job as 'stalled'

    dashboard_polling: |
      GET /api/activity returns activity status for all courses.
      Includes stalled_count and list of stalled course codes.
      Dashboard can use this to alert operator or trigger respawn.

    build_status: |
      GET /api/build/status/:courseCode returns:
      - is_active (from build_jobs DB record)
      - build_mode ('parallel')
      - heartbeat_alive (boolean)
      - progress (completed, total, percent)
      - parallel info (total_drafts, valid, collision, rework)

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SEED GRID UI
  ## ==========================================================================

  seed_grid_ui:
    title: "Visual Build Progress in Dashboard"
    component: "src/views/production/TextGeneration.vue"

    data_source: |
      GET /api/build/seed-grid/:courseCode
      Queries course_seeds (decomposed_at), course_legos (count per seed),
      course_practice_phrases (count per seed), and course_seed_drafts
      (validation_status per seed).

    grid_rendering: |
      A flex-wrapped grid of 5x5px colored cells, one per seed up to
      the course's seed_count. Each cell's color reflects its status.
      Hover shows tooltip with seed number, status, LEGO count, and phrase count.

    color_mapping:
      complete: "bg-emerald-500/80 — decomposed_at is set (live tables)"
      drafted: "bg-amber-500/80 — valid draft in staging"
      collision: "bg-red-500/80 — collision or rework status"
      rework: "bg-red-500/80 — same visual as collision"
      building: "bg-slate-700/80 — has LEGOs but no decomposed_at (partial)"
      empty: "bg-slate-700/80 — no content"

    header_counters:
      - "{finalized}/{total} finalized"
      - "{drafted} drafted (amber, shown if > 0)"
      - "{collision} collision (red, shown if > 0)"

    rebuild_controls: |
      The grid section includes rebuild controls (From/To seed number inputs
      with a Rebuild button) that wipe LEGOs and phrases for a seed range
      via POST /api/build/rebuild/:courseCode, enabling targeted re-decomposition.

    polling: |
      fetchSeedGrid() is called periodically during active builds to show
      real-time progress as agents submit drafts and finalization occurs.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## API ENDPOINTS
  ## ==========================================================================

  api_endpoints:
    title: "Parallel Build API Surface"

    build_start:
      method: "POST"
      path: "/api/build/start/:courseCode"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Start a parallel build with coordinator agent spawning"
      body: "{ terminal: 'iTerm2', targetSeeds: 668 }"
      response: "{ ok, course_code, job_id, progress, build_mode: 'parallel' }"

    build_stop:
      method: "POST"
      path: "/api/build/stop/:courseCode"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Stop an active build"

    build_status:
      method: "GET"
      path: "/api/build/status/:courseCode"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Get build status including parallel draft progress"

    seed_grid:
      method: "GET"
      path: "/api/build/seed-grid/:courseCode"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Seed status grid for dashboard visualization"
      response: "{ seeds: [{seed, status, legos, phrases}], total, complete, drafted, collision, building, empty }"

    seed_complete_draft:
      method: "POST"
      path: "/api/seed/complete?draft=true"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Submit seed decomposition as draft (parallel mode)"
      note: |
        Same endpoint as non-draft submission but with ?draft=true query param.
        Skips ZUT validation (deferred to finalize).
        Skips checkpoint gate.
        Uses translation-based vocabulary instead of LEGO-based vocabulary.
        Upserts into course_seed_drafts instead of live tables.

    drafts:
      method: "GET"
      path: "/api/course/:code/drafts"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "List draft status summary for coordinator polling"
      params: "?status=valid|collision|rework (optional filter)"
      response: "{ course_code, total_drafts, valid, collision, rework, drafts: [...] }"

    finalize:
      method: "POST"
      path: "/api/course/:code/finalize"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Process all drafts into live tables with collision detection"
      response_success: |
        HTTP 200: { ok: true, status: 'FINALIZED', seeds_written, legos_introduced,
        legos_deduplicated, empty_seeds, phrases_written, collisions: 0 }
      response_collision: |
        HTTP 409: { error: 'COLLISIONS_DETECTED', collisions: [...],
        colliding_seeds: [...], resolution: { steps: [...] } }

    heartbeat:
      method: "POST"
      path: "/api/heartbeat/:courseCode"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Agent heartbeat for stall detection"

    activity:
      method: "GET"
      path: "/api/activity"
      port: 3471
      purpose: "Activity status for all courses (stall detection)"
      response: "{ courses: {...}, stalled: [...], stalled_count, threshold_minutes: 5 }"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## KEY DESIGN DECISIONS
  ## ==========================================================================

  design_decisions:
    title: "Rationale for Architectural Choices"

    draft_table_not_queue: |
      Drafts use a table with UNIQUE(course_code, seed_number) rather than
      a queue. This means resubmission (upsert) replaces the previous draft
      for that seed. There is no draft history — only the latest submission
      matters. This simplifies collision resolution: fix agents just resubmit,
      and the old draft is overwritten.

    zut_deferred_not_skipped: |
      ZUT checking is not removed for parallel builds — it is deferred from
      submission time to finalization time. At submission, each agent cannot
      see other agents' drafts, so checking would give false negatives.
      At finalization, all drafts are processed in seed order against a
      single growing baseline, giving accurate collision detection.

    seed_order_finalization: |
      Drafts are processed in seed_number order during finalization.
      This matters because:
      1. Lower seeds' LEGOs become baseline for higher seeds' dedup checks
      2. Empty seed detection depends on knowing all prior vocabulary
      3. Deterministic results regardless of agent submission order

    translation_based_vocab: |
      Parallel agents validate phrase vocabulary against seed translations
      (target_text of seeds 1..N-1) rather than LEGOs. This works because
      LEGOs must tile their seed translation, so word-level vocabulary is
      identical. This avoids agents depending on each other's LEGO output.

    coordinator_is_lightweight: |
      The coordinator agent is an orchestrator, not a builder. It spawns
      sub-agents, monitors progress, calls finalize, and handles collision
      resolution. It uses Sonnet model for cost efficiency. Sub-agents
      also use Sonnet for quality decomposition.

    golden_seeds_excluded: |
      Seeds 1-10 are golden (hand-verified calibration seeds already in
      live tables). Parallel builds start from seed 11. The coordinator
      brief explicitly states "Seeds 1-10 are golden (already done)".

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SUMMARY
  ## ==========================================================================

  summary:
    principles:
      - "Parallel builds use a coordinator -> sub-agents -> draft staging -> finalization pattern"
      - "Drafts are staged in course_seed_drafts, isolated from live tables"
      - "ZUT collision detection is deferred to finalization, not skipped"
      - "Finalization processes drafts in seed order for deterministic results"
      - "Collisions are resolved by upchunking ambiguous words into M-LEGOs"
      - "Smart batch assignment skips seeds with existing valid drafts or finalized status"
      - "Dashboard seed grid shows real-time progress with color-coded statuses"
      - "Heartbeat and stall detection keep builds resilient to agent crashes"
      - "The coordinator runs unattended — designed for overnight builds"

    key_files:
      - "services/course-builder-api.cjs — all parallel build logic"
      - "database/migrations/20260207_course_seed_drafts.sql — draft table schema"
      - "database/migrations/20260208_add_build_mode_to_build_jobs.sql — build_mode column"
      - "src/views/production/TextGeneration.vue — seed grid UI component"

